Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/lib/tlssrp_depr.c
Line: 126
Function: set_up_srp_arg
Bug type: use-after-free
CWE: CWE-416
Explanation: SSL_CTX_set_srp_cb_arg(ctx, &srp_arg) stores the address of a stack-local pointer variable. After set_up_srp_arg returns, this pointer becomes dangling. Later, SRP callbacks (e.g., ssl_give_srp_client_pwd_cb and ssl_srp_verify_param_cb) cast the arg to SRP_ARG* and dereference it, causing a use-after-scope/use-after-free and invalid memory access. The correct argument to store is srp_arg, not &srp_arg.

